
%9Syntax:%9

@SYNTAX:upgrade@

%9Parameters:%9

    The location of the new binary; if no arguments are given, the current
    binary file will be used.

%9Description:%9

    Upgrades to a new version without disconnecting from non-SSL servers; please
    bear in mind that it does not download or compile a new version.

    The state of the connections goes to the file session in the erssi
    directory, which the new process reads. When it cannot be written (a
    full disk or quota, a directory erssi cannot write to), nothing is
    upgraded: erssi says why and goes on with its connections. Found
    before the save, as it usually is, nothing was closed; found only by
    the write at the end, the connections over TLS have already been quit
    for the upgrade and connect again.

%9Examples:%9

    /UPGRADE
    /UPGRADE /home/mike/irssi-dev/bin/irssi

%9See also:%9 CONNECT, DISCONNECT, HELP

